DETAILED ANALYSIS
======================================================================

Interesting observations from the results:

1. EMT Results:
   - Optimized bond length: 0.9981 Å (experimental: 1.0980 Å)
   - EMT underestimates bond length by 0.0999 Å
   - Atomization energy: 9.9372 eV (overestimates by +0.18 eV)

2. MACE Results:
   - Optimized bond length: 1.1124 Å (experimental: 1.0980 Å)
   - MACE overestimates bond length by 0.0144 Å
   - Atomization energy: 10.3130 eV (overestimates by +0.55 eV)

3. Method Comparison:
   ✓ MACE gives better bond length (error: 0.0144 Å vs 0.0999 Å)
   ✓ EMT gives better atomization energy (error: 0.1772 eV vs 0.5530 eV)

4. Conclusion:
   While MACE was expected to be more accurate for both properties, the results show:
   - MACE gives significantly better bond length (only 1.31% error vs 9.10% for EMT)
   - However, EMT gives surprisingly good atomization energy for N₂ (only 1.82% error)
   - This demonstrates that simple empirical potentials can sometimes give good results
     for certain properties, even if they are less accurate overall.

